<img src="/images/johan-gant-566.jpg" srcset="/images/johan-gant-320.jpg 320w, /images/johan-gant-566.jpg 566w" sizes="(min-width: 768px) 320px, (min-width: 368px) 320px, calc(100vw - 48px)" width="566" height="529" alt="Johan Gant" fetchpriority="high" class="block h-auto w-full max-w-80">
<div class="max-w-lg space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
<p>Based on the edges of the Antrim Glens in Northern Ireland, I'm a software developer by trade and working with metal in a creative way gives me a counterbalance to digital life by both producing tangible, physical things but also refining my techniques and understanding of materials and tools. This site is a small collection of that work.</p>
<p>I’ll be sharing finished pieces alongside the process: the experiments, the details, and what I learn as I go.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-16 md:px-12" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
<div class="grid items-start gap-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,2fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] md:gap-12">
<div>
    <h2 id="approach-title" class="font-serif text-3xl">What's with the name?</h2>
    <p class="text-lg">
    Three Paw Forge takes its name from our resident farm cat, Patch, who came to live in our shed around the winter of 2020. Independent, fond of a sunny spot, and usually somewhere nearby while I work, she’s the three-pawed character behind the name.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5"><a href="/about/patch/" class="inline-block py-2 font-bold">Meet Patch — her story and photographs →</a></p>
    <p class="mt-8 text-lg">
        Three Paw Forge is not a big operation. I created it out of one half of my home garage using materials from a kitchen refit that I turned into a workbench, anvil table and shelves making a small but functional workshop space.
    </p>
</div>
<figure class="w-full max-w-60 md:justify-self-end">
